  Quote of the Week:

  Desierius Erasmus, Dutch scholar, 1521:
  "Let a King recall that to improve his realm is better than to increase 
his territory."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  Stormy winter gave way to sweet spring.  Kahn sailed into the Jellyfish 
Sea (#1105) with his forces.  Looking to the southeast, one espies a Forest 
area, which is known as Falkenheim (#1106).  It is populated by Eagles and 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll rules there.  If need be, they can muster 
an army of Eagles to defend their territory.  Southwest of here is the 
Dolphin Sea (#1006), a rich Forest area ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll, where Elves dwell.  Their Elven warriors 
traditionally fight as Bowmen and Heavy Cavalry.

  Soldiers carrying the battle-standards of the Kahnian empire marched on 
the Forest province of the Jellyfish Sea, a land defended by the soldiers of 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll (#1).  Kahn was in command of the 
attacking armies.  The defending forces were commanded by the provincial 
garrison commander.  The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown 
here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of the Jellyfish Sea (1105):

  88th/S            
