  DEFENDING ARMY

  II Kahn marched with his loyal troops, eyes set in grim resolution.  No 
generals were present to lead the forces of Uga-Buga Makumb.
  As luck would have it, Kahn's formations were well concealed by some 
rocks, giving them a small edge.  As the fierce battle intensified, the 
tactical abilities of the acting commander and Kahn seemed evenly matched 
and neither leader could gain a tactical advantage.

  Out on the left wing, the 214th Fleet Marines faced the 287th Garrison.  
The 88th Garrison outflanked the enemy lines and charged in with full 
strength.  Here, when the commander of the 214th Fleet Marines noticed a 
weak point in the enemy line, he quickly assembled an elite force of picked 
veterans to break through it, and achieved some initial success.
  The struggle blazed with a terrible fury.  The 287th Garrison used 
wide-headed catapult missiles to cut down the enemy's catapult engines.  The 
214th Fleet Marines fought with the 287th Garrison and gradually gave 
ground.
  Out on the right outside wing, the 87th Garrison were aided in the battle 
by a band of medicine men from the League of Pagan Clerics, which aroused 
them to a fanatical zeal.  They faced the 288th Garrison.  Here, the 
soldiers of the 288th Garrison were held up by a muddy field.
  But then the tide turned.  The commander of the 87th Garrison was 
flattened by a boulder thrown from a catapult, which terribly deflated the 
spirits of the troops.  The 87th Garrison fought the 288th Garrison and was 
forced to retreat in disarray.
  Having found a vulnerable point in the line of the host of Kahn, a final 
savage slashing attack defeated their enemy and won the battle for the 
acting commander.  The 288th Garrison annihilated the 87th Garrison.
  Kahn's armies were defeated and pushed out of the Jellyfish Sea.  The 
214th Fleet Marines and the 88th Garrison were unable to retreat and were 
paroled into the general population.

  An army coming from the empire of Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll 
invaded Sherwood, hoping to subjugate that province owned by II Kahn and 
made up of great Forests.  Odysseus (#97)'s forces encountered little 
opposition in Sherwood and Odysseus there established our rule.  Odysseus 
leads approximately 2 Bowmen, 4 Dragons, 2 Eagles and 1 Trolls.
  Windy spring blossomed into early summer.  Kahn could not recruit Axemen 
in the Jellyfish Sea because Kahn does not own that province, and 
mercenaries weren't available.  So, Kahn invented nothing in his sagely 
researches.
  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Bradipo I (#2) (whose 
alliances are too incompatible) and Kahn, degrading their diplomatic 
relations 1 level(s)!
  With the advent of the late summer season Kahn could not leave army 88, 87 
and 214 because those soldiers weren't owned by his kingdom.  Instead, he 
invented nothing in his sagely experiments.
  The summer mellowed into a colorful fall.  Kahn rode into Falkenheim.  
East of here lies the province of Hollabrand (#1206), ruled by 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll.  It is known to be a Forest province 
inhabited by Humans.  Their Human warriors traditionally array themselves as 
Legion and Chariots.  Viewing the southeastern horizon, one can see a 
Mountain province known as Florence (#1207).  It is said that 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango is the ruler there.  It is known to be 
occupied by Dwarves.  Their Dwarven warriors fight in the style of Axemen 
and Light Cavalry.  To the southwest there is a Forest province known as 
Mare Tarkium (#1107), a poor land of Dragons where 
Shaman Uga-Buga Makumb Stuffy doll reigns.  They can call on an army of 
Dragons to defend their territory.
  During early winter, Kahn moved into Florence.  East of here is Jutland 
(#1307), a Mountain area owned by Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango, where 
Orcs dwell.  Their Orcish warriors fight as Bowmen.  Turning to the 
southeast, one espies a rich Mountain area, which is known as Piratum 
(#1208).  It is populated by Orcs and Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango rules 
there.  Their Orcish warriors array themselves in the style of Phalanx and 
Warg Riders.  To the southwest lies a Plain area named the Maldive Sea 
(#1108), populated by Humans.  It is ruled by 
Lord Babba Sissoko Master orango.  Their Human fighters array themselves as 
Legion and Heavy Cavalry.

  Thus endeth the adventures of II Kahn for this year.


  Kahn urged Bradipo I to improve diplomatic relations with his Kingdom, 
speaking at length of the great advantages of such an agreement.  After some 
deliberation, the offer was graciously accepted by Bradipo I.
  Kahn treated with his ally Cosmic Herderer Mugai (#3).  Kahn treated with 
his ally Hokuto (#4).  Kahn treated with his ally Prometeo (#5).  Kahn 
treated with his ally Giovanna (#7).  Kahn treated with his ally Circe (#8). 
Kahn treated with his ally Agesilao (#9).

  Here is the financial report for Kahn's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 5 gold in revenue.  3 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  1 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Kahn was left with 37 gold in the 
treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Hawkins
To: Kahn

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season I prepared to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I journeyed to Sherwood.
  Windy spring blossomed into a fragrant early summer.  I could not recruit 
Light Cavalry in Sherwood because Kahn does not own that province, and 
mercenaries weren't available.  Instead, I worked hard on my Illusions but 
was frustrated in my self-improvement efforts.
  Midsummer's night passed and a pleasant late summer came.  I travelled to 
Bronzeleaf.
  In fall, I rode into Bir Nzaran.
  With the coming of the early winter season, I moved into Mare Ionium.

  Thy humble servant,   Hawkins


